 ## Changelog
+- 2026-10-17 (2): Pregen fixed + faster (screenshot: `Pregen: 0 chunks (tap to stop)` for minutes). Compiled and tested in a Linux scratch crate (rustc 1.75, real `lod.rs` + `world/gen`, stubs for wgpu / atlas / mesh): `lod::tests::*` 12 of 12 pass; the full `mc-rs` crate (wgpu 26) still needs a real build on the phone / CI.
+    - Root cause: the single `lod` worker ran `pregen_step` only when its job queue was EMPTY, and `Lod::update` refills `MAX_PENDING` view builds every frame (~510 tiles in view), so the queue was never empty and pre-generation never ran (old code, test `pregen_runs_while_the_view_is_busy`: 0 chunks after 120 s; now 1.3 s).
+    - Now: `pregen_threads()` = cores / 2 clamped 1..3 threads `lod-pregen<i>` (Voxy World Gen's `maxActiveTasks`), each with its own generator (made at its first tile). `claim` (`DistanceGraph.findWork`) takes the nearest tile that is neither done nor taken (`Shared::pg`: `done` / `busy`), the thread reads its file or `make_tile`s it with trees and sends `Msg::Made` to the worker, which `accept`s it (real chunks laid over, file written, counted 16 chunks, `made` -> re-mesh). A view build that made the tile first wins. Stops by itself when nothing is left; `Drop for Lod` ends the threads. `Msg::Wake`, `pregen_step` and the `try_recv` branch are gone; `Store::make` is the free `make_tile`.
+    - Measured on a desktop: 55 ms a tile with trees (release); a phone is ~10-20x slower, so ~1 s a tile a thread. UNVERIFIED on a device: heat with 3 threads (lower the clamp in `pregen_threads`), memory.
+    - ponytail: a pregen tile generates 36 chunks and populates 25 for its 16 (neighbours redo the margin); threads poll the switch every 100 ms; no thread priority.
 - 2026-10-16 (2): Pregen button + persistence (Voxy World Gen's pre-generation; the first LoD patch compiled and ran, the screenshots still showed guessed trees floating in the air and the user asked for the Voxy feature itself). Written WITHOUT a toolchain again: not compiled, not run; `cargo test --lib --release lod` / `touch_ui` first (`a_tile_file_round_trips`, `pregen_goes_nearest_first_and_counts_chunks` new; `a_cell_keeps_...` changed).
     - Pause menu, top-left: `Pregen: off, N chunks` / `Pregen: N chunks (tap to stop)` (`LayoutRects::pregen`, `PointerRole::Pregen`, `TouchUi::take_pregen`, `Lod::toggle_pregen` / `Lod::pregen`). On: the worker (`pregen_step` = `DistanceGraph.findWork`) makes the tile nearest the player that is not real yet within `RADIUS` (a tile = Voxy's 4 x 4 chunk batch) with its trees, 16 chunks a tile, one per loop turn; a waiting view build or ingest goes first. Stops by itself when the range is done. The tiles it makes are meshed again (`made` channel -> `dirty`) when they were drawn as a guess.
     - Persistence (`ChunkPersistence`): tiles with trees are written to `<world>/lod/<x>_<z>.lod` (`Store::flush`, after every job; temp file + rename; runs of equal columns, magic `L2` + world type + trees; another type or a cut file is ignored) and read back by `Store::tile` before generating, so pre-generation survives a restart and ingested edits are kept. A world reset wipes the folder with the rest.
